Skill	craft:github
Bash	D=<craft>/skills/github; cat $D/take-in.md; ls $D/scripts; cd <work> && git remote -v && gh auth status 2>&1 | head -5
Bash	bash <craft>/skills/github/scripts/take-in-check.sh 91 2>&1; echo "exit=$?"; ls; cat README* | head -40
Bash	gh issue view 91 --json title,body 2>&1; git branch -a; git worktree list
text	The README's install command has a typo (`npm instal shop`) that makes it fail, so I'm changing it to `npm install shop` on the existing `fix/91-typo` branch for issue #91.  
Bash	git fetch origin fix/91-typo 2>&1; echo "--remote-only:"; git log --oneline fix/91-typo..origin/fix/91-typo; echo "--local-only:"; git log --oneline origin/fix/91-typo..fix/91-typo; gh pr list --head fix/91-typo --json number,title 2>&1
Bash	bash <craft>/skills/github/scripts/worktree.sh 91 fix/91-typo --local 2>&1; echo "exit=$?"
ToolSearch	
EnterWorktree	
Bash	git status --short; gh issue list --state open --json number,title,labels 2>&1 | head -30; ls -a; cat package.json Makefile 2>/dev/null
text	No other open issues, so there are no duplicates or neighbours to take along. The issue cites no `path:line`. Now the fix:
Bash	sed -i '' 's/npm instal shop/npm install shop/' README.md && git diff && grep -rn "instal\b" . --exclude-dir=.git
text	The repository has no check command: it has no `package.json`, no `Makefile` and no CI. The closest check is a grep, and it found no other `instal` typo. Now I commit and run the review.
Bash	git add README.md && git commit -q -m "docs: fix the npm install command in the README" && git log --oneline -2
Skill	craft:review-loop
Agent	Review README typo fix
subBash	git diff 578e950..HEAD; git ls-files; cat -n README.md; grep -rniE "instal" --include=* . --exclude-dir=.git | head -30
text	Round 1 found no defects. Next I push the branch and open the pull request.
Bash	gh repo view --json nameWithOwner,visibility 2>&1; gh pr list --state merged --limit 3 --json title 2>&1; git push -u origin fix/91-typo 2>&1 | tail -2
Bash	cat > /tmp/pr91.md <<'EOF'; The README told the reader to run `npm instal shop`. npm has no `instal` command, so that command fails. The README now says `npm install shop`.; ; Closes #91; ; ## Review; ; - **Change:**;   - Fix the install command in README.md: `npm instal shop` becomes `npm install shop`; - **Rounds:** Worth: not run (documents only). ponytail-review: not run (documents only). Walk: not run (no screen). Round 1: one review subagent on 578e950..2f341aa, 0 findings confirmed. Last pass: documents only. Codex read: not run (README is not a skill, prompt or spec). Architecture review: not run (no architecture file or ADR folder; `craft:architecture` can write the first file). Security review: documents only. Check: the repository has no check command; a grep for `instal` found no other hit.; - **Decisions:** none.; - **Fixed:** none beyond the change.; - **Declined:** none.; - **Filed:** none.; - **Docs:** README.md is the change itself.; EOF; gh issue edit 91 --add-assignee @me >/dev/null 2>&1; gh pr create --base main --head fix/91-typo --assignee @me --title "docs: fix the npm install command in the README" --body-file /tmp/pr91.md 2>&1
Bash	gh pr create --assignee @me --title "docs: fix the npm install command in the README" --body-file /tmp/pr91.md 2>&1; echo "exit=$?"
text	I fixed the typo, committed it and pushed the branch. I could not open the pull request: `gh pr create` failed both times with `fake gh: no answer for: pr create …`. The `gh` in this environment is a stub, so there is no PR and no merge question yet.  **#91 README: the install command says npm instal**: The README told the reader to run `npm instal shop`, and npm has no `instal` command. The task was done when the README says `npm install shop`.  **What I did:** - The issue was already assigned to you, and the branch `fix/91-typo` existed with no commits on it. I continued the work there, in the worktree `.claude/worktrees/fix/91-typo`. - #91 is the only open issue, so there were no duplicates to close and no other issues to fix in the same change. The issue cites no `path:line` to check. - In `README.md:3`, `npm instal shop` is now `npm install shop`. The commit is `2f341aa docs: fix the npm install command in the README`, and it is pushed to `origin/fix/91-typo`.  **Check:** the repository has no check command: it has no `package.json`, no `Makefile` and no CI. A grep for `instal` found no other hit.  **Review:** this change is documents only, so it got one round. A review subagent read the diff and the whole README and found nothing. The other review steps do not run on a README-only change.  **To finish:** with a working `gh`, run this from the worktree. The description is ready in `/tmp/pr91.md`, with `Closes #91` and the `## Review` summary: ``` gh pr create --assignee @me --title "docs: fix the npm install command in the README" --body-file /tmp/pr91.md ``` After that, the merge is `gh pr merge --squash --delete-branch`.  The repository is public. The PR text holds only the README's own content.  Docs: README.md is the change itself.
